                         According to BCF results calculated in terms of heavy metal concentrations obtained from
                         sediment, heavy metals were biosorbed in the plant as Hg > Cd > As > Zn > Pb > Mn > Ni >
                         Cr > Cu > Al. Plants take toxic heavy metals as well as micro-macro and functional nutrients
                         into their tissues through their roots from sediment in order to carry out their biological
                         functions. While Zn, Mn and Cu are micro nutrients for plants, Ni and Al are regarded as
                         functional nutrients23. Therefore, according to BCF results based on sediment in this study,
                         specifically toxic heavy metals displayed accumulation in the plant (Figure 3).




