                  3 Materials and methods
                  The workflow (Fig. 3) adopted in this study follows a systematic approach to investigate
                  arsenic contamination and mobilization mechanisms in groundwater. It begins with
                  the selection of the study area based on literature review, followed by field surveys and
                  sampling site selection. Both groundwater and soil samples were collected, properly pre-
                  served through acidification and refrigeration, and then subjected to laboratory analyses

