                                 (Fig. 1) across the region could likely be due to the cation exchange of Ca2+ and Mg2+ for Na+. Moreover, Na+
                                 ions are likely be derived from feldspar and clay mineral weathering within the aquifer systems31, a process that
                                 releases Na+ into the groundwater. The detection of SO42− in small number of samples indicates the possible
