data/evidence/autonomy/codex-runs/codex-sprint-2026-05-30T04-49-56-098Z.log:3763:Notes: 9 source pages ingested from Papers Cube Manual Fetch. fu2019 (B-tier): human metabolism review covering As/Pb/Cd/Hg/Ni mechanisms; useful for health pages but over-emphasizes drinking water vs dietary exposure. khan2015 (A-tier): comprehensive food plant bioaccumulation review with transfer factor data (leaf > root > grain hierarchy; Cd TF 1–10 in leafy veg; As into rice via phosphate transporters); essential supply-chain and ingredient-page reference. gomez-arroyo2017 (A-tier): dandelion biomonitor in Mexico City metropolitan area; higher metals in dry season; Al dominant at Altzomoni; V dominant at urban CCA; useful for atmospheric deposition and seasonal variance context. meng2023 (B-tier, CC BY): electrochemical sensor review in Food Control; covers SWASV/DPASV, AuNP/graphene/Fe₃O₄ composites; LOD benchmarks for Pb/Cd/As in food matrices vs WHO/China limits. sharma2023 (B-tier, CC BY): Frontiers phytoremediation review covering phytoextraction, phytostabilization, phytovolatilization, rhizofiltration; MT/PC/HMA molecular mechanisms; relevant to mitigation/agronomic page. si2024 (B-tier, CC BY): Frontiers Chemistry mini-review adding colorimetric (AuNP-aptamer) and fluorescent (quantum dot) detection alongside electrochemical; complementary to meng2023, more recent. kalicharan2025 (C-tier): pet food ICP-OES study South Africa (n=31); classified C-tier (not human food); mean dog food: As 7.47, Cd 6.23, Pb 3.99, Hg 0.47, Ni 16.72 mg/kg; red meat > poultry > fish for most metals. ali2024 (B-tier, conference): leek contamination Iraq (n=100); soil Ni 94–101, Cu 44–62, Pb 20–21 µg/g; highest Zn in plant tissue 28.41 ppm summer; limited HMT&C relevance but geographic variance context. guan2014 (C-tier): 3-page Chinese conference paper, qualitative background only, no original data. SKIPS (per task instructions): pasumpon2021, pollard2016, article (2) copy (wastewater), Heavy Metals in Infant Clothing, mathew2015. New-page proposals: none (all relevant destinations are existing pages).
